{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00045",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.98,
      "end_seconds": 4.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Hi, doctor. Long queue outside, but here I am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.42,
      "end_seconds": 11.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Of course, put it down anywhere. So, how can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.14,
      "end_seconds": 22.84,
      "duration_seconds": 10.7,
      "text": "Yeah, it's cramping pain in the lower tummy. I don't know what's causing it. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.48,
      "end_seconds": 25.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.92,
      "end_seconds": 35.12,
      "duration_seconds": 8.2,
      "text": "I mean, I'm not sure when it began, to be honest. Some weeks ago, but I can't say how many."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.52,
      "end_seconds": 38.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "How bad is it, would you say?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.74,
      "end_seconds": 54.86,
      "duration_seconds": 16.12,
      "text": "I'd say moderate. I've also had a feeling of not emptying fully, for six months. Hmm, uh, with feeling of not emptying fully, it's severe, honestly. And I've been passing a lot of wind as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.41,
      "end_seconds": 61.81,
      "duration_seconds": 5.4,
      "text": "Have you had cramping pain in the lower tummy before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.67,
      "end_seconds": 68.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.84,
      "text": "Oh, a bit, about six months ago. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.23,
      "end_seconds": 71.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Are you comfortable? Do you want some water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.42,
      "end_seconds": 76.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Yes, some water would be nice, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.59,
      "end_seconds": 79.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "And night-time diarrhoea, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.79,
      "end_seconds": 83.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "No night-time diarrhoea, thank goodness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.99,
      "end_seconds": 87.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Have you had any fever, blood in the stool or anaemia?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.95,
      "end_seconds": 91.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Hmm, nothing like that, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.05,
      "end_seconds": 95.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.68,
      "end_seconds": 99.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Hmm, no, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.82,
      "end_seconds": 102.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.97,
      "end_seconds": 104.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "No, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.51,
      "end_seconds": 109.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just scrolling back through your chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.48,
      "end_seconds": 110.32,
      "duration_seconds": 0.84,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.51,
      "end_seconds": 129.37,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.27,
      "end_seconds": 132.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "No, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.09,
      "end_seconds": 137.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "Sorry, the computer needs a moment to load this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.44,
      "end_seconds": 139.29,
      "duration_seconds": 0.85,
      "text": "No rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.0,
      "end_seconds": 157.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.66,
      "end_seconds": 171.96,
      "duration_seconds": 9.3,
      "text": "I take omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.37,
      "end_seconds": 175.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Right, how long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.52,
      "end_seconds": 184.45,
      "duration_seconds": 7.93,
      "text": "About about a year. So, it's escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day. It's Colospa, when it cramps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.92,
      "end_seconds": 189.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.58,
      "end_seconds": 191.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "My brother has asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.89,
      "end_seconds": 202.91,
      "duration_seconds": 11.02,
      "text": "I like to make sure you understand what's happening, so please stop me at any point. There are no silly questions, and I'd much rather you ask now than go home still wondering about something."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.44,
      "end_seconds": 206.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Right, I understand now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.75,
      "end_seconds": 212.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.71,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.84,
      "end_seconds": 224.04,
      "duration_seconds": 10.2,
      "text": "Yes, acid reflux. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible. I have anxiety. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.58,
      "end_seconds": 225.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.77,
      "end_seconds": 240.79,
      "duration_seconds": 14.02,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.91,
      "end_seconds": 243.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.43,
      "end_seconds": 247.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "One moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.82,
      "end_seconds": 248.57,
      "duration_seconds": 0.75,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.49,
      "end_seconds": 259.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.77,
      "end_seconds": 263.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "Can I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.76,
      "end_seconds": 266.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Breathe in deeply... and out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.0,
      "end_seconds": 285.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Soft tummy, a bit tender on the left lower side, no masses."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.34,
      "end_seconds": 307.1,
      "duration_seconds": 18.76,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Good, that's all I need to examine. Let me gather my thoughts and then we'll talk it through together. From what you've told me and what I found, this looks most like irritable bowel syndrome as a working diagnosis. It could also be a food intolerance, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.76,
      "end_seconds": 309.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Doctor, is this dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.88,
      "end_seconds": 330.49,
      "duration_seconds": 16.61,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with irritable bowel syndrome as a working diagnosis do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had cramping pain in the lower tummy, moderate, and no night-time diarrhoea or fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 332.0,
      "end_seconds": 335.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Hmm, exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.48,
      "end_seconds": 349.8,
      "duration_seconds": 14.32,
      "text": "What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 351.34,
      "end_seconds": 353.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.78,
      "end_seconds": 356.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "I'm going to order a stool calprotectin, for bowel symptoms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 358.27,
      "end_seconds": 360.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "The earliest is Monday, 3:30 pm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 361.36,
      "end_seconds": 372.05,
      "duration_seconds": 10.69,
      "text": "We should do a coeliac test for bloating. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. Let's get blood tests, for bowel symptoms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 373.08,
      "end_seconds": 373.99,
      "duration_seconds": 0.91,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 376.65,
      "end_seconds": 403.46,
      "duration_seconds": 26.81,
      "text": "Note down what you ate before the bad days, it often reveals a pattern. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. Please don't sit on it if the symptoms get worse. That's the point to get seen urgently. I'd like to see you again in six weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 404.75,
      "end_seconds": 410.82,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "Before we finish, can you repeat the plan back to me so I know I haven't been confusing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 412.02,
      "end_seconds": 416.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "So, I come back in six weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 419.17,
      "end_seconds": 424.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Good. Call the clinic if you need us in the meantime."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 425.34,
      "end_seconds": 428.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "That's everything I wanted to ask. Thank you."
    }
  ]
}